      nanos: 340165982
    }
  }
  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing App Design**\n\nI\'m currently focused on dissecting the application\'s design and its modular structure. The primary objective is to build a robust, production-ready application for Food Waste Prevention & Control (Gest\303\243o e Preven\303\247\303\243o do Desperd\303\255cio Alimentar) in Portuguese.\n\n\n**Detailing User Requirements**\n\nI\'ve moved on to a detailed examination of each user requirement, focusing on the \"Waste Log\" feature. Specifically, I am defining fields such as food waste type, category, quantity, estimated cost, time, location, responsible user, and more. This also involves quick presets, custom entry modals, and an interactive history table with search and filtering capabilities.\n\n\n**Defining Loss Insights**\n\nI\'m now focusing on defining loss insights by sector (Kitchen, Plating, Storage, etc.). I plan to create an interactive module illustrating both \"Money lost\" and \"Potential savings with reduction actions\" (e.g., 30%, 50%, or 70% savings with optimization). I will also integrate dynamic calculations, such as illustrating the loss from fish (e.g., 120 kg \303\227 12\342\202\254/kg = 1.440\342\202\254).\n\n**Outlining Performance Metrics**\n\nI\'ve outlined crucial Key Performance Indicators (KPIs). This encompasses waste in kg per day (moving average), waste in kg per meal (e.g., 150g/meal vs. 80g target), waste percentage (based on total weight served/purchased), monthly evolution (comparison to the previous month), associated CO\342\202\202e emissions (with a conversion factor of ~2.5 kg CO\342\202\202e / kg food), and progress towards a reduction target (e.g., reduce 25% by the year\'s end).\n\n**Implementing Smart Alerts**\n\nI am now developing automated alerts. These include warnings for products nearing expiration (3 days, 1 day, and today), alerts for exceeding waste limits (e.g., waste surge alerts for Fish/Meat), excessive purchasing or over-allocation, and deviations from the average.\n\n\n**Defining Stock Management**\n\nI\'m now detailing stock management and FEFO (First Expire, First Out) rotation. I\'m focusing on an active stock table that includes lot codes, expiration dates, quantities, and storage temperatures. I am also working on FEFO indicators, recording stock movements, and setting up expiration notifications to promote prioritized use or donation.\n\n\n**Expanding Reporting Capabilities**\n\nI\'m now detailing automated reports and export functionalities. I am focusing on monthly sector and category reports, trend charts, category breakdowns, comparative bar graphs, and Excel (.csv) and PDF export options for easy analysis and presentation.\n\n\n\n**Predicting Waste Trends**\n\nI\'m now integrating AI-driven predictions. I am calculating waste risk based on meal history and day of the week, with smart purchasing suggestions to prevent overstocking. I\'m analyzing consumption trends to identify potential surpluses. I am also planning an interactive AI assistant for waste prevention, serving as a HACCP and sustainable chef consultant.\n\n\\n\\n\n\n**Visualizing Dashboard Components**\n\nI\'m currently focusing on the design of the main dashboard and integrated visual modules. This includes a real-time summary of waste for the day and month, economic losses, CO\342\202\202 emissions, and reduction targets. I\'m also planning a dynamic module highlighting potential savings. I will include a monthly waste trend chart, a list of the top 10 most wasted products, and a prioritized feed of alerts.\n\n\n**Designing Core Components**\n\nI\'m now focusing on integrating initial data in Portuguese. It will include realistic waste logs, FEFO items, donations, and non-conformities. I\'m building a modern header with quick stat badges, navigation, and AI integration. The dashboard will feature metrics, loss visualizations, trend charts, and alerts. I\'m also developing modals for waste logging, economic analysis, and stock management.\n\n\n**Developing Module Functions**\n\nI\'m now focusing on specific module functions. I\'m actively developing components for donation registration and partner directories, compost and recycling logs with sustainability metrics, HACCP non-conformities and traceability features, and AI-driven forecasts, including surplus predictions and a chat advisor. I am also working on monthly executive reports with export options, and the design for system alerts for issues like expiration or waste threshold breaches.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 10
      nanos: 375459635
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
