  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Data Models**\n\nI\'m now creating `/src/types.ts` to implement the data models. The initial focus is on the `WasteCategory` interface, and I\'ve reviewed the requirements to include categories like \'Carne\', \'Peixe\', \'Frutas\', \'Legumes\', \'Lactic\303\255nios\', \'Padaria\', and \'Refei\303\247\303\265es Confecionadas\'.\n\n\n**Expanding Data Structure**\n\nI\'ve expanded the `WasteCategory` enumeration to include the entry \'Outros\'. I\'m also adding `WasteType`, `ProductionLocation`, `WasteLog`, and `StockItem` interfaces, along with their respective properties and data types, to the data model. I\'m taking care to define the specific types for units (kg, L), dates (YYYY-MM-DD), and times (HH:mm) as well. I am including fields to calculate the total cost and CO2 emissions.\n\n\n**Defining New Structures**\n\nI\'m now focusing on defining new interfaces. Specifically, I am adding `StockMovement`, `DonationLog`, `ValorizationLog`, and `HaccpLog` structures to the data model. I will define types for fields like quantity and date, as well as the string literals such as \'Entrada\', \'Sa\303\255da\', and \'Compostagem\' for their respective fields.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 7
      nanos: 844434485
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
